From c74510756b4c387c5cc1795788b507d7cf9373ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:38:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Persist operator actions: manual incidents, field edits,
 notes, event ACK

Previously these only lived in the frontend store and were overwritten by the
next backend refresh (i.e. on the next WebSocket message).

Backend
- POST /api/v1/incidents: open an incident manually (ID from the same
  sequence as correlated incidents; counts toward the vessel score).
- PATCH /api/v1/incidents/{id} is now partial: status, severity,
  assigned_operator, investigation_notes, actor (all optional).
- POST /api/v1/incidents/{id}/notes: append an investigation note.
- POST /api/security-events/{event_id}/acknowledge; event responses carry
  "acknowledged".
- Incident responses include "notes" and "timeline". The timeline is an
  append-only audit trail (incident_activity): opened by correlation/manual,
  each operator change with before/after values, notes added.
- New tables incident_notes, incident_activity, event_acknowledgements
  (created by create_all; Alembic migration 20260924_0004 included).
- WebSocket messages: incident_created, event_acknowledged.

Frontend
- services.ts applies changes optimistically, then persists them through the
  new endpoints; if the backend is unreachable the local change is kept.
- Events are keyed by event_id instead of the numeric DB id, so an incident's
  "Related events" list now actually shows its events.
- Notes and timeline are rendered from the backend data.

Tests: tests/test_incident_workflow.py.

